            "review_title": "Review at La Baguette",
            "review_text": "SARAH S K\n22 contributions\n0\nHidden Gem\nDec 2025 • Couples\nThis is a hidden gem. We decided to stay a night in the intercontinental after a cruise in HLB. Right now with the new build they only had Marina and La Baguette so we decided to have dinner there. \n\nFirst they had baguette service and bread was fresh warm and delicious. Served with truffle butter and salt. \n\nThen we had foie gras- delicious combinations of all flavors from the chutney with jelly and salad lightened the richness of the foie gras, everything worked so well together with the brioche which was perfectly made. We also tried the Hokkaido French onion soup and the baguette that came with was amazing. Perfectly toasted with delicious butter- good bread here hence the name of the restated. The soup was a bit different in that cheese was light on top and smaller scallops but many. This was not our fav but still enjoyed it.\n\nOn to the main, black chicken was delicious. Deboned, delicately presented with thigh and breast with sticky rice with shrimp. Both were flavor bombs that was a perfect fusion of French culinary technique and bold flavors of Vietnam. This was cooked, prepared, seasoned and presented perfectly. Sauce was amazing- I think it could use a side of pickle for Asian palette.\n\nWine selection is wonderful. tasty.\n\nLastly service was so amazing. Attentive, amicable, builds rapport and cares for quality. \n\nAmazing!!\nRead more\nWritten December 14, 2025\nChi N\nXin chao SARAH S K,\n\nThank you very much for your kind and detailed feedback.\n\nWe are delighted that you chose to dine with us during your stay and are honored to be considered a “hidden gem.” It is wonderful to know that you enjoyed our freshly baked baguette service, foie gras, and especially the black chicken with sticky rice, which reflects our fusion of French technique and Vietnamese flavors. We also truly appreciate your thoughtful comments regarding the soup and your suggestion, such insights are invaluable to us.\n\nYour compliments on our wine selection and, most importantly, our attentive service mean a great deal to the entire team.\n\nWe sincerely look forward to welcoming you back for another incredible dining experience.\n\nSincerely,\nJesper Bach Larsen\n\nGeneral Manager\nInterContinental Halong Bay Resort\nRead more\nWritten February 12, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
